[8:48:02 AM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  Analyzing commit: fix(release): default release base to the branch the workflow runs on

semantic-release determines the current branch from the CI env (GITHUB_REF
= the dispatch ref), then checks it against --branches. Hardcoding the base
to 'development' only matched when dispatched on development; dispatching on
test/development gave --branches development vs CI branch test/development →
'won't publish' → empty version → step failed. Defaulting base to
github.ref_name keeps --branches in sync with the dispatch branch in both
shadow (test/development) and post-flip (development).
