[8:48:02 AM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  Analyzing commit: fix(multisig): handle out-of-order proposal events when approveProposal=true (BE-144)

When createProposal is called with approveProposal=true, the Approved event is emitted
before ProposalCreated in the same transaction. The approved handler misses the vote
because the proposal doesn't exist yet. After creating the proposal, the handler now
scans the same transaction for missed Approved/Executed events and processes them.
