[8:48:02 AM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  Analyzing commit: fix(rates): exclude fdv_usd from dead token market data check (#1249)

* fix(rates): exclude fdv_usd from dead token market data check

Tokens with inflated pool prices (zero volume, null market cap) were
passing the dead token filter because fdv_usd is derived from
price_usd × total_supply — making it non-zero even when the price
is fake. Only market_cap_usd (independently tracked by CoinGecko)
is a reliable signal of a legitimate token.

* feat(admin-api): add token price refresh endpoint via RabbitMQ

POST /queue/token-price/:tokenAddress/:network forces an immediate
CoinGecko price refresh by publishing to the tokenInfo queue with
forceUpdate=true, processed by aragon-gateway.

